From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 13:31:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06949/11362] [outer-loop] Task 13 MoE follow-on:
 Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MTP vs frozen generator (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5597)

Follow-on to exp5596 (dense 27B). Downloaded and verified unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MTP-GGUF
(21.6GB Q4_K_M, genuine qwen35moe.nextn_predict_layers=1 MTP support). Reused exp5596's
self-draft VRAM feasibility check unmodified: MoE sparsity does not relax the self-draft
problem (the full weight file is still loaded twice regardless of active-parameter count), so
self-draft is again infeasible on a single 24GB 3090. A manual non-MTP single-load sanity check
confirmed the model fits with only ~2.2GB headroom before running the real A/B.

Real result is the OPPOSITE direction from exp5596: honest_verdict
generator_size_ab_equal_success_current_higher_accuracy -- the MoE candidate scored LOWER (mean
heldout_accuracy 0.65) than the current 9B generator (mean 0.75) on the same m0r0+sk48 roster,
and was substantially slower (67.3s/14.4s vs 1.5s/0.7s induce time). The current generator's own
baseline scores differ between the exp5596 and exp5597 runs despite identical config -- real LLM
sampling variance, documented explicitly, not a bug.

Honest combined reading across both A/Bs: neither candidate has demonstrated a reliable
induction-quality edge over the current generator at n=2 games per arm -- exp5596's positive
signal and exp5597's negative signal could both be sampling noise. A larger roster and/or
multiple seeds per (game, arm) would be needed before either direction is trustworthy enough to
inform an operator decision. The frozen live-submission generator remains unchanged.

